{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02LB", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:23ab09006b1e611f5483bc40acaff303bb3f6ac14bb2960428c27a86984717c5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe can reformulate the hypotheses in the lemma above a bit by using the\nfollowing characterization of flat universally injective morphisms.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:031a4ffa2585672cd5ba416274fd266f1d65d7031b461edece33322699f572eb", "unit_id": "tag:02LB:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02LB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$X^0$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\xi \\in X^0$", "MATH_0006": "$\\kappa(f(\\xi)) = \\kappa(\\xi)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\xi, \\xi' \\in X^0$", "MATH_0008": "$\\xi \\not = \\xi'$", "MATH_0009": "$f(\\xi) \\not = f(\\xi')$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-flat-universally-injective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ad47f855323b611dcee190ef1915dbafcd098a7b5ee1516dbc3ce8f9b53157e6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:126d888565753dc4d52c1626556519d3368d4ed2de8c08545dd0e9fac4021958", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. Let <MATH_0002> denote the set\nof generic points of irreducible components of <MATH_0003>. If\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is flat and separated,\n<STRUCT_0003> for <MATH_0005> we have <MATH_0006>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> if <MATH_0007>, <MATH_0008>, then <MATH_0009>,\n<STRUCT_0005>\nthen <MATH_0010> is universally injective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:38f5ac029c24ee58a4cb2a220566bd522c3ed84183394d44d060089c122ccbd7", "unit_id": "tag:09NP:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02LB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Delta : X \\to X \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0005": "$\\eta \\in X \\times_S X$", "MATH_0006": "$X \\times_S X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0008": "$\\text{pr}_1 : X \\times_Y X \\to X$", "MATH_0009": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0010": "$\\text{pr}_1$", "MATH_0011": "$\\xi = \\text{pr}_1(\\eta) \\in X^0$", "MATH_0012": "$(X \\times_Y X)_{f(\\xi)}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\xi \\in X^0$", "MATH_0014": "$\\Delta(\\xi) = \\eta$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-universally-injective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-base-change-flat}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-generalizations-lift-flat}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d31b0d77d868873b4e1023a353af48f94e2f653c6e75f2fe697625889075e0b4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3d95afa6638a6d0c2e834ca49296c7ed7c19ba3e40c5d4a37ce32b7815f22e9a", "source_text": "We have to show that <MATH_0001> is surjective, see\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nAs <MATH_0002> is separated, the image of <MATH_0003> is closed.\nThus if <MATH_0004> is not surjective, we can find a generic point\n<MATH_0005> of an irreducible component of <MATH_0006>\nwhich is not in the image of <MATH_0007>. The projection\n<MATH_0008>\nis flat as a base change of the flat morphism <MATH_0009>, see\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nHence generalizations lift along <MATH_0010>, see\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nWe conclude that <MATH_0011>.\nHowever, assumptions (2) and (3) guarantee that the scheme\n<MATH_0012> has at most one point for every <MATH_0013>.\nIn other words, we have <MATH_0014> a contradiction.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b797c7c11fe0fdc0351770344bb6380e313ab3deba186111ce341d86e140245e", "unit_id": "tag:09NP:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02LB", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-universally-injective-etale-open-immersion}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dc71b429af4a2b21bb3fb563d34371ded428d1245a11f856c70360b694943c5a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThus we can reformulate\nLemma <REF_0001> as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:97efdbab57d4d15c4d98c4c7a6e5e379246549e5b1b8606e25930e42de6563fd", "unit_id": "tag:02LB:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02LB", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$X^0$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\xi \\in X^0$", "MATH_0006": "$\\kappa(f(\\xi)) = \\kappa(\\xi)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\xi, \\xi' \\in X^0$", "MATH_0008": "$\\xi \\not = \\xi'$", "MATH_0009": "$f(\\xi) \\not = f(\\xi')$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-open-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ad47f855323b611dcee190ef1915dbafcd098a7b5ee1516dbc3ce8f9b53157e6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:102898a7323f6b2fb26237915975bb1b714d3c73875edb4a56765dd089d2a2bf", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. Let <MATH_0002> denote the set\nof generic points of irreducible components of <MATH_0003>. If\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is <ACCENT_0001>tale and separated,\n<STRUCT_0003> for <MATH_0005> we have <MATH_0006>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> if <MATH_0007>, <MATH_0008>, then <MATH_0009>,\n<STRUCT_0005>\nthen <MATH_0010> is an open immersion.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:512225cb48755b120b536ac8cf4d650cbbfc538800f7119a7272812890556f85", "unit_id": "tag:09NQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02LB", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-flat-universally-injective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-universally-injective-etale-open-immersion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8adba35a08a815f9f5205b9280fbe764f1ac3a952770cd6a8d2afb743053f362", "source_text": "Immediate from Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9fcddfdb2bc8372dd72198512635f4bd53bea445c88b2045920c8ecdb24ba99d", "unit_id": "tag:09NQ:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02LB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$Z$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{Y_i \\to Y\\}$", "MATH_0005": "$Z_i \\subset Y_i \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0006": "$Y_i$", "MATH_0007": "$Z$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{coherent-definition-proper-over-base}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-proper-over-base}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c8795e6baf2d3006d989c35d85d52b75fd567eb6e0037f149414087520ef33c5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b6096a0f9d62297d50123af4869bf957b87bafdc8d3f8261bb2ec342398a65a6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite type.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a closed subset of <MATH_0003>. If there exists an fpqc covering\n<MATH_0004> such that the inverse image <MATH_0005>\nis proper over <MATH_0006>\n(Cohomology of Schemes, Definition <REF_0001>)\nthen <MATH_0007> is proper over <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eb817872a24008e9c0bba5a15423d37ad89814afebe8ec38cb2ff72c1eb82d31", "unit_id": "tag:0F4J:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02LB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Z$", "MATH_0002": "$i$", "MATH_0003": "$Y_i \\times_Y Z$", "MATH_0004": "$Y_i \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0005": "$Z_i$", "MATH_0006": "$Y_i \\times_Y Z \\to Y_i$", "MATH_0007": "$Z \\to Y$", "MATH_0008": "$Z$", "MATH_0009": "$Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-definition-reduced-induced-scheme}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{coherent-lemma-closed-proper-over-base}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-proper}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:67105f689014eca88a5f8c58c7fd50338857371cd0932930ffc917ad58b976f7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dc4f0e562b417ae9b0af178a1ca8495e4d256098983b525bfd6d410030a87527", "source_text": "Endow <MATH_0001> with the reduced induced closed subscheme structure, see\nSchemes, Definition <REF_0001>.\nFor every <MATH_0002> the base change <MATH_0003> is a closed subscheme\nof <MATH_0004> whose underlying closed subset is <MATH_0005>.\nBy definition (via\nCohomology of Schemes, Lemma <REF_0002>)\nwe conclude that the projections <MATH_0006> are proper\nmorphisms. Hence <MATH_0007> is a proper morphism by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nThus <MATH_0008> is proper over <MATH_0009> by definition.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b829c90f24da7e23e392aa78894a30d10db680b6ce8f205778c01583d677acbb", "unit_id": "tag:0F4J:proof"}
